{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.ContentCasimir","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ContentCasimir","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QJucysMurphy"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.contentCasimir_rhoTriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.contentCasimir_rhoTriv","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/ContentCasimir.lean#L142-L159","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.contentCasimir_smul_of_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.contentCasimir_smul_of_weight","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/ContentCasimir.lean#L101-L127","doc":"**Block eigenvalue of the content Casimir.**  If every Murphy element `L_k` (`k ≤ n`) acts on\n`v` by `a_k²`, with `a_k b_k = 1`, then `C_n` acts on `v` by `Σ_k (a_k − b_k)(q·a_k − qi·b_k)`,\nwhich is `(q − q⁻¹)² Σ_k [c_k][c_k+1]` when `a_k = q^{c_k}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_smul_of_qJM_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_smul_of_qJM_smul","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/ContentCasimir.lean#L86-L99","doc":"The inverse Murphy element acts on a weight vector by the inverse eigenvalue: derived from\n`qJMInv_mul_qJM`, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.contentCasimir_comm_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.contentCasimir_comm_σ","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/ContentCasimir.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**`C_n` is central**: it commutes with every Hecke generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.contentCasimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.contentCasimir","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/ContentCasimir.lean#L67-L72","doc":"**The content Casimir** (denominators cleared by `(q − qi)²`):\n`C_n = q·Σ_{k≤n} L_k + qi·Σ_{k≤n} L_k⁻¹ − (n+1)(q + qi)` in `H_{n+1}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.cell_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.cell_identity","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/ContentCasimir.lean#L60-L65","doc":"**Per-cell identity.**  With `a·b = 1` and `q·qi = 1`, the cleared symmetric product\n`(a − b)(q·a − qi·b)` — that is `(q − q⁻¹)² [c][c+1]` at `a = q^c` — equals `q·a² + qi·b² − (q + qi)`,\na Laurent polynomial in the Murphy eigenvalue `a²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}